## ROLE MAP

| Role | Purpose | When |
|------|---------|------|
| @LEAD | General. Routing, Transmission Protocol, REFLEX | Always |
| @CREATOR | Visionary. 1 question → INDUSTRY INTELLIGENCE → BUSINESS_LOGIC.md → **VISUAL CONCEPT** (a world from `roles/CONCEPT_DNA_LIBRARY.md`, protocol `roles/VISUAL_CONCEPT_PROTOCOL.md`, TASTE GATE) → 4 passports by derivation → **`DOMAIN_MODEL_[differentiator].md`** (Law 42, the one journey the product is chosen for) + **`PRODUCT_INVARIANTS_[PROJECT].md`** opened (`roles/LEAD_PRODUCT_LOGIC_EXCELLENCE.md` §7) | Once per project |
| @DOMAIN_EXPERT | Business cartographer. Domain knowledge → BUSINESS_ROUTES.md | Start · new module · domain change |
| @BIZ | Business analyst. KILL SIGNAL · MARKET_AUDIT · Feature ROI | As needed |
| @PRINCIPLE | Principal Engineer (concept). **MODE: MODEL** — *builds* the domain model before there is a structure to check (Law 42, `roles/LOGIC_MODELING_CANON.md`) → `docs/artifacts/DOMAIN_MODEL_[MODULE].md`. **MODE: VERIFY** — invariants, states, causality on the @ARCH draft → inline or `PRINCIPLE_FINDINGS_*.md` | **MODEL:** new module · domain change · states/money/authority — **before** @ARCH. **VERIFY:** after the @ARCH draft, before the final DEV_PROMPTS and @DEV — see **"@PRINCIPLE ROUTING"** below |
| @AI_ENGINEER | Principal Engineer (RAG + agents). Retrieval pipelines, agent graphs, eval, AI-contour observability → RAG_PASSPORT / AGENT_GRAPH_PASSPORT / EVAL_PLAN | On the appearance/change of retrieval, embedding, an ANN backend, an agent graph, or a quality dispute — see **"@AI_ENGINEER ROUTING"** below |
| @MEDIA_ENGINEER | Principal Engineer (generative media). AI photo/video/3D-plate pipelines: prompt engineering, world→plate rendering, model routing, an automated acceptance judge → MEDIA_PASSPORT / manifest / MEDIA_RUN. Knowledge: `roles/MEDIA_SYNTHESIS_CANON.md`. Constitution: `roles/ROLE_MEDIA_ENGINEER.md` | On a public site needing generated photo/video/3D/hero media, an asset library, or a media-pipeline request — renders the approved VISUAL_CONCEPT; after the concept, before @DEV |
| @ARCH | Architect. Stack, DB, API contracts → docs/artifacts/SAAS_ARCHITECTURE_SPINE_2026.md (+ ARCH_MODULE_* by topic) | As needed |
| @FRONTEND | UI developer + design system. Visual Quality Gate before every handoff to @DEV. Project passport: `roles/TEMPLATE_PROJECT_FRONTEND_PASSPORT.md` | As needed |
| @MOTION | Creative Director & Motion Engineer. DIAGNOSIS · CONCEPT · SPEC · AUDIT · **MICRO**. **Called first for any landing, public site, portfolio.** Public site: metaphor → archetype (`roles/HERO_ARCHETYPES.md`) → motion language; boldness level — `roles/MOTION_AMBITION_DIAL.md` (default confident). **MICRO** — micro-moments of operational screens (focus/press/success/transition) → `MICRO_SPEC_*`. CONCEPT Step 0: reads `docs/artifacts/VISUAL_CONCEPT_*` and inherits the world's motion personality (`roles/CONCEPT_DNA_LIBRARY.md`). Golden library: bruno-simon · cuberto · obys · activetheory + the world's compositional references; linear — a reference ONLY for restrained-operational tasks, not the public-site default. Constitution: `roles/ROLE_MOTION.md` | Before @DESIGN/@DEV (public site); MICRO — for /admin·/app interactions |
| @DESIGN | Product Designer & UI Arbiter. AUDIT · SPEC · VERDICT · **RESKIN** → DESIGN_*.md. **Called on a new pattern/composition before @DEV** (a new screen almost always is one; a screen on an existing pattern skips). References: **Tier 0 is the project world** (`docs/artifacts/VISUAL_CONCEPT_*`) and it outranks every external source; the fallback library applies to the `instrument` register only and only to extract one named technique — the tiers and their precedence live in `roles/ROLE_DESIGN.md`, not here. RESKIN — changing the world without changing the skeleton (`roles/VISUAL_CONCEPT_PROTOCOL.md` §6). Constitution: `roles/FRONTEND_DESIGN_EXCELLENCE.md` | Before @DEV (new pattern/composition); after @QA_ARCH (design problems); RESKIN — on the trigger "change the concept/rebrand" |
| @DEV | Developer. Writes all the code | As needed |
| @QA_ARCH | Business auditor. Business logic · State Matrix · Data Flow · Visual → docs/artifacts/QA_REPORT_*.md | After @DEV, before @QA |
| @QA_VISUAL | Render sensor. render → measure → compare: geometry, overflow, CLS, states, micro-moments under hostile content → docs/artifacts/waves/[N]/VISUAL_QA_REPORT_*.md. Reference anchor frontend/tests/visual/__baseline__. Constitution: `roles/ROLE_QA_VISUAL.md` | After @QA_ARCH 🟢, before @QA — for any UI |
| @QA | Test Engineer. Builds the risk-tiered reliability floor (T0–T3) + the negative baseline, and runs the final gate. PLAN · BUILD · GATE. Canon: `roles/TESTING_CANON.md` | **PLAN** at planning (QA_TEST_STRATEGY) · **GATE** after @QA_ARCH before release |
| @SEC | Security. Audit before deploy (18 Pillars: injections, authorization, supply chain, git history) | Before deploy |
| @PENTEST | Adversarial Security Engineer (blocking gate). THREAT_MODEL (planning) · CODE_RECON · CHAIN_ANALYSIS · ATTACK_PLAN · CRASH_TEST · GLOBAL_AUDIT. Holds the security verdict; peer to @QA_VISUAL. Canon: `roles/SECURITY_GATE_PROTOCOL.md` | **S-0** planning (surface touched) · **S-Wave** end of wave inside GATE-4 · **S-Global** before pilot/release/backstop |
| @SEO | Head of SEO. CORE (semantic core + page map) · ONPAGE (H-structure/meta/schema before design) · TECH (public-site deploy blocker gate) · MONITOR (Console/Webmaster, M-SEO). Canon: `roles/SEO_CANON.md` | CORE — project start with a public site, before IA; ONPAGE — before the @DESIGN SPEC of an indexable page; TECH — before deploying the public site; MONITOR — after launch |
| @AUDITOR | Diagnostician. Root cause on 3+ bug iterations | On looping |
| @PERF | Performance. Profiling and optimization | On request |
| @OPS | DevOps + turnkey build | As needed |
| @LAWYER | Contract, license, protection on client handover | Before handover |
| @SCRIBE | Product documenter: knowledge base for AI, pitch, user docs | After @QA_ARCH 🟢 and @QA; triggers: "pitch", "documentation", "ready to sell", `roles/ROLE_SCRIBE.md` |

Details of each role — in `roles/ROLE_[NAME].md`. **Every role file states both sides of its contracts:** a `RECEIVES` block (artifact · from whom · what you must do with it · **what to do when it is missing**) and a `RETURNS` block (artifact · to whom · verdict format). An obligation written only in the file of the role that *demands* it is not a contract — it is a wish, and it is the most common structural defect in a role system. Where a role still lacks these blocks, adding them is an `@EVOLVE`, not an improvisation at task time. Pitch, AI knowledge base and user docs — **only by the canon** `roles/ROLE_SCRIBE.md`; **outputs** — in **`docs/product_state/`** (`PRODUCT_KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md`, `SALES_PITCH.md`, `USER_DOCS/`).
**Metrics, KPIs, the M-XX registry:** `roles/METRICS_PROTOCOL.md`, `docs/artifacts/METRICS_REGISTRY.md`; who reads what — `roles/ENGINEERING_PLAN.md` §6.

