## PROJECT MEMORY (sources of truth by layers P / S / W)
> **Git boundary:** `roles/` — fully in `.gitignore`, not committed, does not go to the client. `docs/` — committed in full; RAG history, artifacts and product_state are kept in the repo; handed to the client selectively by @LEAD's decision. `documentation/` — the public layer, goes to the client.
> **In git (public):** only **`documentation/`** — see `documentation/README.md`; where to write user and product texts — **`documentation/SCRIBE.md`**. **Closed layer (`.gitignore`, does not reach clients):** the internal RAG and roles — `roles/RAG_CANON.md`, `roles/ENGINEERING_PLAN.md` §5 · `docs/product_state/README.md` · **`docs/product_state/RAG_NAVIGATION_S_LAYER.md`** (the reading order of layer S for RAG) · `roles/SYSTEM_FILES_MASTER.md` (A). Do not embed a link to the restructuring plan into every `ROLE_*.md`.

### Layer P — process norm (`roles/` — the closed layer, not in git)
- `roles/ROLE_*.md`, `roles/ENGINEERING_PLAN.md`, the LEAD protocols, templates, passports
- **`roles/RAG_ARCHITECTURE_STACK_2026.md`** — the canon of the RAG stack and pipelines (ingestion, retrieval, evaluation); mandatory for tasks on the knowledge base and document generation with an AI contour
- `roles/DOMAIN_STANDARDS.md` — the minimum standard for each page type by domain (§0 infrastructure, §1–§7 module, §8 domain extensions)
- **`roles/PRODUCTION_READINESS_CANON.md`** + **`roles/PLANNING_MATURITY_CANON.md`** — production-ready by default (Law 41): the bar (foundation complete / delivery phased), the self-audit loop DRAFT→RED-TEAM SELF-PASS→REFINE, the Completeness Ledger + spot-check, and the three criteria (responsibility · foresight · completeness)
- **`roles/SECOND_PASS_PROTOCOL.md`** — the clean-context audit pass: why a fresh window finds what the producing chat cannot, the three levels SP-1/SP-2/SP-3 and the SP-0 interceptor, the role set per task class, **the derivation chain** (what each artifact is checked against — this is what turns re-reading into checking), the known false-green catalogue FG-1…FG-12, and the boundary that stops a pass from silently reconstructing what it audits. Not automatable by design; @LEAD plans its slots into every series
- **`roles/LOGIC_MODELING_CANON.md`** — the modeling core (Law 42): seven layers of a domain model, the finite catalogue of twelve adversaries, the terminating cycle, the `DOMAIN_MODEL_[MODULE].md` artifact and its gate. Read by @PRINCIPLE (MODE: MODEL), @LEAD (gate), @ARCH (derives structure from it), @CREATOR (first model of the differentiator journey), @QA_ARCH (model ↔ code reconciliation)
- **`roles/CONFLICT_REGISTRY.md`** — resolved cross-file conflicts and their single winners (anti-drift; every `@EVOLVE` overlap adds a row and syncs the mirrors)
- `roles/TEMPLATE_ADMIN_UI_UX.md` — the UI/UX template for operational screens (`/admin`, `/app`)
- `roles/TEMPLATE_DESIGN_UX.md` — the UI/UX template for marketing pages (`/`, landings)
- **`roles/SYSTEM_DESIGN_PROTOCOL.md`** — design for load: Load Profile, Latency Budget, Bottleneck Analysis, Failure Modes, Queue/Cache/Mobile/AI design
- **`roles/DATA_STORE_SELECTION.md`** — the store-selection canon: PostgreSQL, Redis, MongoDB, TimescaleDB, ClickHouse, Kafka, pgvector, Qdrant
- **`roles/STACK_SELECTION.md`** — the global stack: Python/Java/Go/Mobile/AI/K8s
- **`roles/DEV_EXECUTION_PASSPORT.md`** — the map of @DEV check points + a catalog of 13 code patterns (including Rate Limiting, Security Headers)
- **`roles/ARCHITECTURE_DOCUMENTATION_STANDARD.md`** — the standard for keeping architecture documentation, the ADR registry, onboarding
- **`roles/PENTEST_SCENARIOS.md`** — the library of attacking artifacts: pytest tests, curl commands, locust scripts
- **`roles/ROLE_PENTEST.md`** — Adversarial Security Engineer (blocking gate): the vector tree A–G + T-series, modes THREAT_MODEL/CODE_RECON/CHAIN_ANALYSIS/ATTACK_PLAN/CRASH_TEST/GLOBAL_AUDIT, the **scourge** contract with @ARCH/@DEV
- **`roles/SECURITY_GATE_PROTOCOL.md`** — the process contract that makes security mandatory: the SECURITY SURFACE (S1–S12), the three checkpoints (S-0/S-Wave/S-Global), the Security Contract, GATE-4 integration, narrow risk-acceptance (§4A), red-green regression evidence (Law 38)
- **`roles/FRONTEND_DESIGN_EXCELLENCE.md`** — the taste constitution: the operational contour (§2, Crisp SaaS patterns + code) and the public site (§4); Visual Quality Gate §6 — mandatory for @FRONTEND and @QA_ARCH
- **`roles/ROLE_MOTION.md`** — Creative Director & Motion Engineer: diagnosis, visual metaphor, motion principles, 6 ready code patterns, Motion Quality Gate §5
- **`roles/MOTION_LIBRARY.md`** — the exhaustive arsenal of techniques: typography T1-T6, backgrounds B1-B6, interactivity I1-I5, scroll narrative S1-S4, WebGL W1-W4, transitions, performance rules §VII — read by @MOTION when choosing a concept
- **`roles/LAYOUT_INVARIANTS.md`** — the canon of deterministic layout invariants (equal-height, reserved height, min-width, aspect-ratio, zero-shift, no-layout-animation); verified by @QA_VISUAL
- **`roles/ROLE_QA_VISUAL.md`** — the render sensor: Playwright harness, meters, geometry vectors V1–V12 + V13/V14 detectors + craft floor V15–V20, the baseline reference anchor, the debugging cycle
- **`roles/HERO_ARCHETYPES.md`** — a library of 8 hero/composition archetypes + a selection protocol (removes the "text+mockup" default)
- **`roles/MOTION_AMBITION_DIAL.md`** — the ambition dial (input to @MOTION CONCEPT) + the MICRO mode (micro-moments of operational screens)
- **`roles/FRONTEND_CONSOLIDATION.md`** — the map of single sources of tokens/geometry/direction; the reclassification of TPF_*; the artifact layout
- **`roles/CONCEPT_DNA_LIBRARY.md`** — 12 concept worlds as executable recipes (hex palettes, font pairs with Cyrillic, CSS effect-kits, motion personalities, Mantine skins) + the custom-world Constructor + a niche→world router
- **`roles/VISUAL_CONCEPT_PROTOCOL.md`** — "Concept before code": the birth of the concept @CREATOR (Step 5.5.A/B), TASTE GATE (cliché ban-list C1–C10), the transfer map into 4 passports, the @DESIGN RESKIN mode, model economics
- **`roles/CONCEPT_ANATOMY.md`** — the generative core of taste: 8 concept DNA axes with variant spaces, axis-coherence rules, the reference protocol (extraction criteria), a world constructor for any niche
- **`roles/LAYOUT_COMPOSITION.md`** — the CONSTRUCTION grammar of layout: the three laws of space, the algebra of 8 primitives (Stack/Cluster/Grid/…), the law of proximity as a number, action-group grammar, the collision-diagnosis protocol
- **`roles/ROLE_SEO.md`** — Head of SEO: 4 modes (CORE/ONPAGE/TECH/MONITOR), boundaries with @ARCH/@DESIGN/@DEV, transmission, veto on the public-site deploy
- **`roles/SEO_CANON.md`** — the SEO canon: semantics→IA, rendering (the SSG/SSR table), the technical baseline with CWV budgets, on-page formulas, local SEO, Yandex+Google, AI search, monitoring
- **`roles/ASYNC_WORKERS_CANON.md`** — the async-contour contract: three planes (data/control/supervision), laws AW-1…13, a pattern catalog (Saga/Outbox/Flows/limiter), the JOB PASSPORT and PIPELINE PASSPORT contracts, sizing, crash-tests T-A…T-G + T-I1…I6, anti-patterns AP-1…20 (incident #2: limiter at the wire, lease as the single life clock, single retry owner)
- **`roles/DATA_INTEGRITY_CANON.md`** — integrity under concurrency: the invariant-protection hierarchy, a race catalog with SQL recipes, Idempotency-Key/inbox, money/time/tenancy/deletion-audit, the INVARIANT LEDGER, the T-H tests
- **`roles/ARCH_SPINE_PROTOCOL.md`** — the decision spine: 12 vertebrae as numbers before code, the complexity ladder 0–4 with triggers, the default timeouts/deadlines of the synchronous path, the ARCH_SPINE template
- **`roles/DATABASE_RUNTIME_CANON.md`** — the DB as a live resource (Law 35): guard rails as numbers, session and connection lifecycle, lock discipline and the **corpse-lock pattern**, maintenance isolation, the pulse (the corpse alarm), the "who holds the lock" runbook, tests T-D1…T-D7
- **`roles/ASYNC_AWAIT_REFLEX.md`** — @DEV's grep self-check before shipping: hangs · races/duplicates · transactions+queues (incl. the abandoned transaction holding locks). Mirrored by @QA_ARCH — what @DEV catches itself is not sent back
- **`roles/VISUAL_CRAFT_CANON.md`** — the physics of expensive (Law 33, `REGISTER: instrument`): restraint, the one-separation rule, one light source, the inverse-area chroma law, the modular type scale, optical alignment, the cheapness detector X1–X12, **THE FLOOR §11** (the fully specified default when there is no concept)
- **`roles/EDITORIAL_CRAFT_CANON.md`** — the craft of the STATEMENT (Law 33, `REGISTER: statement`): scale as a weapon, tension and asymmetry, **one gesture committed to completely**, editorial typography (drop cap, baseline grid, pull quote, optical kerning, mixed weights, text as image), the **timidity detector Y1–Y12**
- **`roles/INTERFACE_CRAFT_CANON.md`** — the craft of the instrument: the I1–I12 interaction inventory (command palette · inline edit · bulk · **undo instead of confirm** · saved views · keyboard), trees/folders/repositories, data density, the stiffness detector ST1–ST12
- **`roles/CANVAS_CRAFT_CANON.md`** — node graphs, pipeline builders, agent canvases: typed ports, edge semantics, auto-layout, the inspector, loops with a visible exit condition, **execution as a first-class layer (the run overlay)**, the toy-graph detector G1–G10
- **`roles/FRONTEND_CAPABILITY_CANON.md`** — the CAPABILITY_MAP (Law 34): read the backend before designing over it; C1–C12; the tablecloth detector T1–T10
- **`roles/SYSTEM_EVOLUTION_PROTOCOL.md`** — the `@EVOLVE` command: how the system itself may be changed. **Manual trigger only — the system never edits itself.**
- **`roles/TEMPLATE_PROJECT_FRONTEND_PASSPORT.md`** — the frontend project-passport template (Visual Identity, tokens, modules, live state)

### Layer S — product state (`docs/product_state/`)
- `docs/product_state/RAG_NAVIGATION_S_LAYER.md` — the layer-S navigation scheme (what to read after `INDEX.md`), aligned with `roles/RAG_CANON.md`
- `docs/product_state/PRODUCT_KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md` — the AI-facing canon about the product (@SCRIBE)
- `docs/product_state/SALES_PITCH.md` — the pitch and sales formats (@SCRIBE)
- `docs/product_state/USER_DOCS/` — user documentation without technical jargon (@SCRIBE)
- when it appears: `docs/product_state/openapi.json` (or a name agreed with @ARCH / a README in `product_state/`)
- the metrics registry **M-XX** (INV-6): `docs/artifacts/METRICS_REGISTRY.md` — until a separate move into `product_state/` in one task with all references updated

### Layer W — working tails

**Project canon** — `docs/[project-name]/` (when a dedicated project folder exists): the engineering spec, ADRs, the roadmap, `DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md`, the architecture blueprint, business routes and related documents.

**Development waves and shared artifacts** — **`docs/artifacts/`**:
- `docs/artifacts/BUSINESS_ROUTES.md` — the live map: routes of money, roles, data, critical journeys (with a project folder — also `docs/[project-name]/BUSINESS_ROUTES.md`)
- `docs/artifacts/BUSINESS_LOGIC.md` — what we build and why (with a project folder — also `docs/[project-name]/BUSINESS_LOGIC.md`)
- `docs/artifacts/SAAS_ARCHITECTURE_SPINE_2026.md` — the architecture frame (@ARCH); on a divergence with the **code** or **OpenAPI** — the code is primary (update W/S per `ENGINEERING_PLAN` §5)
- `docs/artifacts/PRODUCT_OPERATING_CORPUS_2026.md` — the product and phases
- `docs/artifacts/SME_BOX_NFR_CHECKLIST.md` — the box NFR
- `docs/artifacts/DEV_PROMPTS_*.md`, `docs/artifacts/QA_REPORT_*.md`, `docs/artifacts/PRINCIPLE_FINDINGS_*.md`, `docs/artifacts/DESIGN_*.md`
- **`docs/artifacts/SEMANTIC_CORE_[PROJECT].md`** · **`docs/artifacts/waves/[N]/SEO_ONPAGE_*.md`** · **`docs/artifacts/SEO_TECH_AUDIT_*.md`** · **`docs/artifacts/SEO_REPORT_*.md`** — the visibility contour (@SEO)
- **`docs/artifacts/JOB_PASSPORTS_[PROJECT].md`** — passports of background-task types (@ARCH approves, @DEV executes line by line; Law 30)
- **`docs/artifacts/PIPELINE_PASSPORT_[pipeline].md`** — the pipeline contract: stages+progress, deadlines, budget/limiter, retry matrix, lease numbers, stuck predicate, T-I (Law 30 v2.0, the "five questions before a pipeline")
- **`docs/artifacts/ARCH_SPINE_*.md`** — the spine of an architectural decision: 12 vertebrae (Law 31; @LEAD gate, @QA_ARCH Spine vector)
- **`docs/artifacts/CAPABILITY_MAP_[MODULE].md`** — what the backend makes possible: C1–C12 surfaced or explicitly not, + what the backend must GROW (Law 34; @FRONTEND produces, @ARCH confirms, @DESIGN consumes)
- **`docs/artifacts/SYSTEM_EVOLUTION_LOG.md`** — the ledger of every applied `@EVOLVE`: why the system is the way it is (SYSTEM_EVOLUTION_PROTOCOL §8)
- **`docs/artifacts/SYSTEM_DESIGN_[PROJECT].md`** — System Design: Load Profile, Latency Budget, Bottleneck, Scaling, Failure Modes
- **`docs/artifacts/ADR_REGISTRY.md`** + **`docs/artifacts/ADR_[NN]_[TOPIC].md`** — the registry and individual ADRs
- **`docs/artifacts/RAG_PASSPORT.md`** · **`docs/artifacts/AGENT_GRAPH_PASSPORT.md`** · **`docs/artifacts/EVAL_PLAN.md`** · **`docs/artifacts/EVAL_RESULTS_[DATE].md`** — the AI contour (@AI_ENGINEER)
- `docs/artifacts/README.md` — the wave-artifacts index (if maintained)
- `docs/artifacts/ARTIFACT_MAP.md` — the artifact map (numbers, levels, archive vs canon)
- the full index and new-file policy — `docs/artifacts/README.md`, `ARTIFACT_MAP.md`

