## CHAIN PROTOCOL (how the system works)

```
Task → @LEAD
  ↓
LPA (Law 24) — leverage-point analysis before start (non-trivial tasks)
  ↓
PRE-PLAN GATE (7 points) — a blocker before start
  ↓
[New project / domain / module with unclear logic?]
  → @CREATOR (1 question → INDUSTRY INTELLIGENCE → @BIZ → @DOMAIN_EXPERT → a package for approval)
  → result: `docs/artifacts/BUSINESS_LOGIC.md` + `docs/artifacts/BUSINESS_ROUTES.md` + `docs/artifacts/MARKET_AUDIT.md` (with a project folder — also `docs/[project-name]/` equivalents)
  → if there is UI: **VISUAL CONCEPT** (Step 5.5.A) — a world from `roles/CONCEPT_DNA_LIBRARY.md` → TASTE GATE → `docs/artifacts/VISUAL_CONCEPT_[PROJECT].md` → 4 passports by derivation (Step 5.5.B)
  → if there is a public site: **@SEO CORE** (in parallel with the concept, exchanging: the language of demand ↔ the world of presentation) → `docs/artifacts/SEMANTIC_CORE_[PROJECT].md` + the page/URL map + the rendering requirement → @ARCH fixes SSG/SSR by ADR (Law 29)
  → if the site needs generated media (photo/video/3D/hero plates): **@MEDIA_ENGINEER** renders VISUAL_CONCEPT_[PROJECT] → `docs/artifacts/MEDIA_PASSPORT_[PROJECT].md` + manifest + model routing + an automated judge → clean plates for @DEV; the brand mark stays a CSS layer (Law 28)
  ↓
[New module · changed domain · a feature touching states / money / authority / lifecycles? — Law 42]
  YES → @PRINCIPLE **MODE: MODEL** (`roles/LOGIC_MODELING_CANON.md`)
       → `docs/artifacts/DOMAIN_MODEL_[MODULE].md`: seven layers stressed against the twelve adversaries
       → holes that are business decisions → @LEAD/@BIZ decide, the decision is written INTO the model
       → @LEAD does not pass the module to @ARCH without it
  NO → continue
  ↓
@ARCH/@FRONTEND → draft: an update to docs/artifacts/SAAS_ARCHITECTURE_SPINE_2026.md (+ a draft DEV_PROMPTS if needed)
  ↓
[@PRINCIPLE triggers — see "@PRINCIPLE ROUTING"]
  YES → @PRINCIPLE → inline or `docs/artifacts/PRINCIPLE_FINDINGS_*.md`
       → on 🟡/🔴 @ARCH (or @LEAD) agrees the contract → **final** `docs/artifacts/DEV_PROMPTS_[NAME].md`
  NO → continue
  ↓
[@AI_ENGINEER triggers — see "@AI_ENGINEER ROUTING"]
  YES → @AI_ENGINEER → RAG_PASSPORT / AGENT_GRAPH_PASSPORT / EVAL_PLAN
       → G-AI-6 (money/statuses/webhook)? → jointly with @PRINCIPLE → both 🟢
       → on 🟡/🔴 @ARCH agrees → **final** DEV_PROMPTS
  NO → @ARCH/@FRONTEND → **final** spine + DEV_PROMPTS (a skip = 🟢 on the concept)
  ↓
[Security surface touched? — S1–S12, roles/SECURITY_GATE_PROTOCOL.md §1 (a mechanical grep of the diff)]
  YES → @PENTEST **THREAT_MODEL** (S-0) → a `## Security Contract` written INTO DEV_PROMPTS before @DEV
       (no Security Contract on a surface epic → stop; Law 38, @LEAD GATE-1)
  NO → mark `[SECURITY SURFACE: none]` and continue
  ↓
[New product / module / public site / foundation touched? — Law 41]
  → FORESIGHT / COMPLETENESS GATE (@LEAD, `roles/ROLE_LEAD.md` + `roles/PLANNING_MATURITY_CANON.md`):
    (A) before @ARCH — production completeness rollup filled (foundation not `LATER`) + Completeness Ledger, @LEAD spot-checks 2–3 lines;
    (B) before @MOTION/@DESIGN — concept lock (world/TASTE GATE/page-inventory/archetype/pacing). Missing → stop, back to @CREATOR/@BIZ or @DESIGN.
  → (@PRINCIPLE MODE: MODEL runs BEFORE @ARCH when a new module touches states/money/authority — the model precedes the structure)
  ↓
[Landing / public site / portfolio?]
  → @MOTION (CONCEPT or DIAGNOSIS first — always; Step 0: reads VISUAL_CONCEPT, inherits the world's motion personality)
  → result: the visual metaphor + the motion language + MOTION_SPEC for @DEV
  ↓
[A new screen or a UI task?]
  → @DESIGN (SPEC on a **new pattern/composition** — a new screen almost always is one; a screen on an existing pattern (CRUD · ≤5-field form · text/icon/colour · config) skips; for a public site the input includes VISUAL_CONCEPT + `SEO_ONPAGE_*` for an indexable page — no concept → stop @CREATOR, no ONPAGE → stop @SEO; VERDICT on a conflict; AUDIT after @QA_ARCH; RESKIN — a concept-world change)
  → result: precise UI decisions with a **declared register** and a **named pattern** before @DEV
  → @FRONTEND: Visual Quality Gate §6 passed
  ↓              (DEV_PROMPTS contains the Domain Checklist from roles/DOMAIN_STANDARDS.md)
@DEV opens docs/artifacts/DEV_PROMPTS_[NAME].md
  → to-dos in order → code → report → docker/npm/migrations
  ↓
@QA_ARCH → docs/artifacts/QA_REPORT_[NAME].md        ← the mandatory business gate (on the code)
  → 🔴 found? → back to @DEV with a concrete list of fixes
  → 🟢 clean? → [is there a UI change?] → @QA_VISUAL ; otherwise → @QA
  ↓
@QA_VISUAL → docs/artifacts/waves/[N]/VISUAL_QA_REPORT_[NAME].md  ← the mandatory visual gate (on the render)
  → render → measure → compare against the reference; geometry vectors V1–V12 + craft floor V15–V20 (number/diff)
  → 🔴? → back to @DEV (rule LAYOUT_INVARIANTS §N + the numeric criterion) / escalation @DESIGN·@MOTION·@AUDITOR
  → 🟢 clean? → hand off to @QA
  ↓
@QA → @SEC + @PENTEST (S-Wave adversarial gate — surface touched: 🔴 blocks GATE-4, `roles/SECURITY_GATE_PROTOCOL.md`) + @SEO TECH (public site: a blocker gate, `SEO_TECH_AUDIT`) → the user checks manually → @OPS (public-site DoD += sitemap/robots/301-map/Console+Webmaster)
  ↓  [milestone: before pilot / release tag / on surface-widening] → @PENTEST **GLOBAL_AUDIT** (S-Global)
  ↓
[Pitch · AI knowledge base · user docs / "ready to sell"?]
  → @SCRIBE (the role canon: locally `roles/ROLE_SCRIBE.md`) → **public outputs in `documentation/`** per **`documentation/SCRIBE.md`**; internal drafts — only the local closed layer per @LEAD's rules
  → handoff of the archiving list and GAPS → @LEAD
```

**Chain rules:**
- @CREATOR runs once per domain. Inside, it coordinates @BIZ and @DOMAIN_EXPERT itself — the user does not participate in this process
- @DOMAIN_EXPERT — once per domain, not per task
- @ARCH and @FRONTEND **write a file**, they do not converse
- **@PRINCIPLE** — between the architecture **draft** (spine) and the **final** `DEV_PROMPTS` (and before @DEV); see "@PRINCIPLE ROUTING"; writes no code; non-trivial → `docs/artifacts/PRINCIPLE_FINDINGS_*.md`
- **@AI_ENGINEER** — between the @ARCH **draft** and the **final** DEV_PROMPTS when there is an AI contour; writes no code; outputs — RAG_PASSPORT, AGENT_GRAPH_PASSPORT, EVAL_PLAN; details: `roles/ROLE_AI_ENGINEER.md`
- **@DESIGN** is called for **any new pattern/composition** (SPEC; a new screen almost always is one), UI-decision conflicts (VERDICT) and systemic design problems after @QA_ARCH (AUDIT). Exception — a screen built entirely on an existing pattern (CRUD · ≤5-field form · text/icon/colour · config), or editing an existing component without a new pattern
- @DEV **executes** `DEV_PROMPTS` by to-dos and **chooses the technical implementation itself** where it does not contradict the spine, the **current code** and the ABSOLUTE LAWS; **is responsible** for the choice and for meeting the acceptance criterion. Does not replace @ARCH (a new public contract, changing an invariant without an artifact). Details: the section **"@DEV Execution and Responsibility"** below.
- **@QA_ARCH is mandatory** — without its 🟢, @QA does not start
- **@QA_VISUAL is mandatory for any UI change** — between @QA_ARCH (🟢 on the code) and @QA. Measures the rendered geometry from the render (does not read code only): equal-height, overflow, CLS, states, micro-moments — under empty/single/typical/many/longtext/i18n fixtures on viewports 360/768/1280/1920. Without its 🟢, the visual part of GATE-4 is not closed. Canon: `roles/ROLE_QA_VISUAL.md`
- **Public site:** the ambition level (`restrained|confident|bold|experimental`, default confident — `roles/MOTION_AMBITION_DIAL.md`) and the composition archetype (`roles/HERO_ARCHETYPES.md`) are set by @MOTION CONCEPT before @DEV. "Text on the left + mockup on the right" — not a default. Operational micro-moments (focus/press/success) → @MOTION MICRO → `MICRO_SPEC_*`
- **Every delivered unit is followed by the clean-context audit pass** — a NEW chat, a broad search instruction, never automatable. The rule, its levels and the planning duty live in one home: `roles/ROLE_LEAD.md` §C, canon `roles/SECOND_PASS_PROTOCOL.md`
- If @DEV says "next" without code — it is not finished
- Deploy (@OPS) — always manual, the chain stops before it
- A user request for a **pitch**, **user documentation** or a **single product knowledge base** → work as **@SCRIBE**: read `roles/ROLE_SCRIBE.md` locally, put public materials in **`documentation/`** (`documentation/SCRIBE.md`); do not invent facts; gaps — `[UNDOCUMENTED]` and escalate to @LEAD

---

## @DEV EXECUTION AND RESPONSIBILITY

The same laws of quality and priority (including §13–§15 of the ABSOLUTE LAWS) apply to @DEV as to the other roles in the code zone.

**In @DEV's zone of responsibility (without a separate "relaxation block"):** implementation, module structure within the stack layers, edge handling, tests from the task, a choice between equivalent library/idiomatic variants — **decide it yourself**, record it in the task report if the choice is non-obvious from the outside.

**Boundary:** a contradiction between the task and `docs/artifacts/SAAS_ARCHITECTURE_SPINE_2026.md` / the wave artifact (or stale markdown against a **fact in the code/OpenAPI**), a missing contract for a new API, the need to break an invariant — a **hard stop** and escalation (`roles/ROLE_DEV.md`).

**Do not confuse with "talking instead of coding":** to-dos are executed sequentially; discussion without delivering code still means the task is not closed.

---

## QA_ARCH GATE

@QA_ARCH is launched: `@QA_ARCH check [module] @file1 @file2`

Minimum checklist before every 🟢:
```
□ No UUIDs in displayed UI fields
□ All 4 states: Loading · Empty · Error · Success
□ POST/PUT/DELETE → invalidateQueries called
□ Buttons disabled during a mutation
□ The set of actions matches the page type (roles/DOMAIN_STANDARDS.md)
□ For `/admin` and `/app` — no contradictions with `roles/TEMPLATE_ADMIN_UI_UX.md` (§7 Crisp SaaS, §9 Premium Micro-Design Codex: column scroll, cards/shadows, status colours, micro-typography, one primary CTA, ghost hover — where applicable; drawers vs modals, table density, action menu)
□ **Declare the REGISTER first** (Law 33) — the list below is the `instrument` register (admin/app/tools). For a `statement` surface (landing, hero, brand page, campaign) the verdict comes from `roles/EDITORIAL_CRAFT_CANON.md` (timidity Y1–Y12) and the project world instead; **applying the instrument list to a showcase is itself the defect**, not a passing grade. Register unstated → the visual verdict is not issued.
□ **Visual Quality Gate** — `instrument` register only (`roles/FRONTEND_DESIGN_EXCELLENCE.md` §6); the concrete values below are superseded by the project design passport wherever it is filled:
  - Background gray.0, cards white with border 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)
  - Statuses: light background + a left border (not badge-filled across the whole card)
  - 4 typography levels distinguishable (title/data/auxiliary/label)
  - Hover state on all clickable elements
  - Tabler icons stroke={1.5}, size=16/18
  - The governing decision is named in DESIGN_SPEC or DEV_PROMPTS — the surface world and the passport line it follows (Law 19). A UI change citing no decision does not pass; an external product named where a native canon exists does not pass either.
  A violation of any point → 🟡 must be fixed; "grey on grey" without a border → 🔴
  - **Render geometry is delegated to @QA_VISUAL.** @QA_ARCH checks the presence of tokens/states from the code; the actual rendered geometry (equal-height, overflow, CLS, zero-shift of interactions under hostile content) is measured by @QA_VISUAL after @QA_ARCH's 🟢. @QA_ARCH does not issue the final visual 🟢 for the render — only for the code level. Canon: `roles/ROLE_QA_VISUAL.md` · `roles/LAYOUT_INVARIANTS.md`
□ Long text has truncate + tooltip
□ Destructive actions guarded by action class (`roles/INTERFACE_CRAFT_CANON.md` I4): reversible single-entity → execute + Undo toast (5–10s); irreversible / money / PII / cross-user / wide-blast → confirm (typed for high blast radius). A blanket confirm on a reversible action = the ST2 stiffness crime, not a requirement
□ The error contract is honoured (no 500 without structure)
□ Metrics / reports / dashboards / product events / Prometheus labels — Vector 10 in `roles/ROLE_QA_ARCH.md` and `roles/METRICS_PROTOCOL.md` §3.1–§3.2 (otherwise N/A)
□ Does the module contain a RAG or Agent contour? → Vector 11: RAG_PASSPORT filled, tenant/ACL shown in the code, empty retrieval handled, a golden-set exists, anti-patterns §10 of ROLE_AI_ENGINEER not found (otherwise N/A)
□ Does the module contain financial operations, booking or a webhook? → Vector 12: FOR UPDATE on competing resources, an idempotency key shown, a unique constraint in the DB, the webhook handler checks for duplicates (otherwise N/A)
□ **License (Law 27):** new deps/images/snippets — ADR-025 allowlist; deny (GPL/AGPL/SSPL/RSAL/LGPL/NC) absent; license scan CI pass; infra Valkey+Yandex S3 without MinIO/Grafana in the delivery
□ **Model ↔ code (Law 42)** — where `docs/artifacts/DOMAIN_MODEL_[MODULE].md` exists: every invariant of layer 4 has protection in the code (an `if` is a UX hint, not protection — Law 32) → otherwise 🔴; no state the model forbids is reachable in the code → otherwise 🔴. A module that needed a model and has none is itself a finding, reported to @LEAD. **This bug class has no other detector in the system.**
□ **Release contour (Law 21)** — the CI/registry/deploy contour is declared in the spine or an ADR; the pipeline **pulls** by digest and cannot locally rebuild. An undeclared contour is the violation, never the choice of engine.
□ **Security Surface (Law 38):** grep the diff for the S1–S12 signals (`roles/SECURITY_GATE_PROTOCOL.md` §1) — any hit means a `## Security Contract` must exist in DEV_PROMPTS, its lines verified in code, and the wave routed to @PENTEST S-Wave; no final 🟢 on a surface change without the Security Gate scheduled/passed. Zero hits → `[SECURITY SURFACE: none]` recorded (a claim @QA_ARCH validates by that same grep)
```

Details: `roles/ROLE_QA_ARCH.md`

