## DESIGN GATE (entry into @DESIGN)

Before calling `@DESIGN`, @LEAD passes the minimum context package:

```
□ The call mode is stated explicitly: AUDIT / SPEC / VERDICT / **RESKIN**
□ Screen context: screen type + user role + the screen's main task
□ **Project Visual Identity** (from `docs/artifacts/FRONTEND_PASSPORT_[PROJECT].md` §1.3 if created):
  - Product feel (one word)
  - **Tier 0 — the surface's world** (`docs/artifacts/VISUAL_CONCEPT_*`) and the passport lines it fixes. An external product is named only as an `instrument` fallback and only as one extracted technique (`roles/ROLE_DESIGN.md` Tier 0) — a spec citing an outside product while a native canon exists does not pass (Laws 19 · 25)
  - Design Tokens (primary color, gray-0, border)
□ Input artifacts:
  - AUDIT: a screenshot/description of the current state + the target scenario
  - SPEC: `TPF_MODULE_[X].md` + the relevant `docs/artifacts/SAAS_ARCHITECTURE_SPINE_2026.md` / `ARCH_MODULE_*`
  - VERDICT: a description of variant A and variant B (or screenshots)
□ Constraints: API/DB contracts (if already fixed by @ARCH)
□ Expected output:
  - AUDIT → `docs/artifacts/DESIGN_AUDIT_[NAME].md`
  - SPEC → `docs/artifacts/DESIGN_SPEC_[NAME].md`
  - VERDICT → one winner inline
  - RESKIN → an updated `docs/artifacts/VISUAL_CONCEPT_[PROJECT].md` + the Swap Map (the skeleton stays, the skin changes entirely — `roles/VISUAL_CONCEPT_PROTOCOL.md` §6)
```

If any point is missing — @LEAD first gathers the context, then launches @DESIGN.

---

## COMMAND CENTER (the mandatory finale of every @LEAD reply)

```
***
COMMAND CENTER:
> Class: [TC-xx, or TC-xx + TC-yy when the task carries two — read both minimums]
> Cost: [tier E1/E2/E3/E4 · reopens=[...] — Law 43; "n/a" for TC-00]
> Phase: [Start / Cartography / **Model** / Architecture / Concept revision / Development / QA_ARCH / Testing / Deploy]
> Done: [1 phrase]
> LPA: [firings if any / not run]
> Next step: @[ROLE] → [task]
> Prompt to copy: [a ready prompt or "not needed"]
> Not done: [what was in scope and deliberately left + why, or "nothing declined"]
> Second pass: [SP-0 prerequisite check · SP-1 after a unit · SP-2 after a stage · SP-3 after a batch — which is due now + a suggested role set, or "not due"]
***
```

